From: mothershipOS
Subject: [PATCH] nio: boot the ADSP at EL2 without QHEE (LPASS bring-up, SID 0x1800, CMD-DB share)

On stock nio, QHEE intercepts the ADSP PAS auth_and_reset (pil_auth_reset_api_ns) and runs
PILSubsys_memAssign -> TZ auth -> PILSubsys_bringUp. TZ alone only authenticates; the hypervisor
clocks the LPASS Q6 and releases it (QHEE hyp-code: lpass_bring_up = ClockSetup(0) + RST_EVB +
ClockEnable(0), recovered by disassembly + unicorn MMIO trace, see ports/nio/docs/audio.md).

- qcom_q6v5_pas: port of QHEE's LPASS bring-up after auth_and_reset (pas_id 1, EL2 only, and only
  when the DT provides the identity SMMU domain and the CMD-DB share; otherwise the Q6 would reset
  the SoC at every boot). Boot vector = mem_phys (image is not relocatable; mem_reloc is its link
  address 0x89500000, which crashes the SoC).
- arm-smmu-qcom: identity domain for qcom,sm8250-adsp-pas (Q6 fetches as apps SMMU SID 0x1800,
  previously a QHEE stage-2 context; blocked unmatched stream -> SoC reset).
- qcom_scm: DT property mothership,el2-cmdb-share-adsp (or qcom_scm.nio_cmdb_share_adsp=1) enables the
  early, kept HLOS+ADSP read-only CMD-DB assignment before SHM bridge enable (TZ rejects it after).
  Generated from the tree the running kernel was built from (it replaces 0016, which no longer applied).

---
